From 8538c3a0a410507129e903de1c60ff69f363642d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:51:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 827/827] fix(dsv41): rename quantization-ignored layers into
 the VL wrapper before layers are built

Upstream base: local-inference-lab/vllm 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354
with candidate-62's series applied through 0826.

Rationale: configure_quant_config renames the modules a quantization config
lists (Fp8Config.ignored_layers) with the model class's hf_to_vllm_mapper,
before the first instance exists. The V4.1 VL wrapper sets its mapper only on
the instance, after its language model has chosen every layer's quantization
method, so the class has none: the list keeps the checkpoint's names
(layers.1.engram.wkv) while the layers are built under the wrapper
(language_model.model.layers.1.engram.wkv). DeepseekV41FP8Config matches
ignored layers exactly, so a projection the checkpoint lists as unquantized is
built block32 FP8. The text-only class already carries a class mapper. Give the
wrapper one holding its module renames only (the five prefixes and the shared
expert's down_proj), from the same tables as the instance mapper; it carries no
tensor, scale or drop rule and needs no model import. The GB10 wrapper
(vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/nvidia/vl_model.py) inherits it.

Quality implications: none on the served checkpoints. DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash
(dba1be0a) and DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017 (1bae0e10) list no ignored layers and
store both Engram projections as E4M3 weights with E8M0 scales, so the list is
empty before and after: every layer's method, the kernels and the outputs are
unchanged. A checkpoint that lists ignored layers now gets them unquantized, as
it states, instead of silently quantized.

Tests: tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_quant_ignore.py in the candidate-61-r2
image on one GB10, with the two files mounted over it: 6 passed. Without the
change to the wrapper, 5 of the 6 fail (the ignored Engram projection gets the
block32 FP8 method); the served-checkpoint case passes both ways.

Upstream status: local; a candidate for vllm-project/vllm, whose wrapper has
the same gap.
